And he ends up singing a song with an inmate that Boswell himself describes as having been very pretty. Boswell is such a dog, isn't he? He then gets drunk with a couple of prostitutes who are wearing red coats in the churchyard of St. Paul's. He's so drunk that he doesn't notice his pocket being picked. He falls over and he has to be helped home by a pair of strangers. and none of this is helping him to write his biography. And it goes on like this. And the months pass and then the years.
