You know, and therefore it has the hint of gossip. And so it's, you know, it's pretty popular. Yeah. And then in 1787, there's a very pompous formal biography, which is claimed to be definitive. And that was written by one of the executors of Johnson's will, a lawyer by the name of Sir John Hawkins. And, you know, it's very stiff. But again, the fact that it's being marketed as definitive, it's a massive, you know, anxiety. for Boswell.
