00:50:40.000 --> 00:51:19.000
And his ambition is as simple as it's hubristic. to write a biography of a kind that has never been written for, to portray Johnson in the words that he ends up putting in his introduction to the biography, more completely than any man who has ever yet lived. So he makes Robert Caro, who writes these 6,000-page books about the life of Lyndon Johnson. He makes him look like a mere pamphleteer, doesn't he? Because Boswell wants to check every fact, he wants to talk to every associate of Johnson's. he wants to write the complete life definitive, no question, unasked or unanswered.
