that Johnson had bought, he made a gift of that to Mrs. Thrail. And Mrs. Strail made a note in her diary, says Johnson, a woman has such power between the ages of 25 and 45 that she may tie a man to a post and whip him if she will. And she then goes on to say, well, I know for a fact that Johnson is aware of this. And just kind of leaves that hanging. So is it a possibility? I mean, I think it's not anachronistic to say it might have been. La Vise Galois, the Welsh vice rears its head again, no?
